@startuml
!theme plain
top to bottom direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Arial

title Persisted Plan / Ticket Lifecycle — Fresh Workers, Shared Plan Branch

state "Plan + child Ticket Issues persisted" as persisted
state "Shared Plan branch active" as branch
state "Main selects dependency-ready Ticket\nCheck dependencies + isolated ownership" as select
state "Fresh Ticket owner\nRetains context across the Ticket" as ticket_owner
state "Owner implements ready Ticket\nLocal checks; integrate before dependents" as implement
state "Optional independent-module helpers\nFixed interfaces + isolated workspaces" as module_helpers
state "Development Complete" as developed
state "Separate fresh Sol/high Ticket verifier\nAll scenarios; read-only" as verify
state "Main coordinator judges Ticket evidence" as accepted
state "More Tickets?" as more
state "Local verified checkpoint\nNormal stopping point; Issues stay open" as local
state "Add same-requirement scope before merge\nUpdate Plan scope/index/dependencies/validation" as expand
state "Final Plan acceptance\nSeparate fresh verifier unless one-Ticket exact-scope coalescing applies" as final_verify
state "Plan integration + Test Quality Gate\nMain coordinator decides" as gate
state "Authorized commit / push / Plan PR actions\nStop at selected boundary" as publish
state "Merge Plan PR once" as merge
state "Delete branch + Update main" as cleanup
state "Close Plan + Tickets" as done
state "BLOCKED\nNo main-agent fallback" as blocked
state "Verification BLOCKED\nRecord cause + resume point" as verify_blocked

[*] --> persisted
persisted -down-> branch
branch -down-> select
select -down-> ticket_owner : fresh independent context + capacity available
select --> blocked : unavailable
blocked -[norank]-> select : capability restored
ticket_owner -down-> implement
ticket_owner --> module_helpers : optional safe independent modules
module_helpers --> implement : integrate isolated patches
implement -down-> developed
developed -down-> verify
verify --> verify_blocked : checks cannot run
verify_blocked -[norank]-> verify : cause resolved
verify -down-> accepted : evidence complete
verify -[norank]-> implement : FAIL: implementation repairs\nthen new verifier; retain failed evidence
accepted -down-> more : Ticket evidence accepted
more -[norank]-> select : yes; fresh owner and verifier for next Ticket
more -down-> local : no
local --> [*] : stop locally; not BLOCKED
local -[norank]-> expand : same-requirement supplement
publish -[norank]-> expand
expand -[norank]-> select : same branch/PR; Plan in_progress\nretain evidence; invalidate impacted readiness
local -down-> final_verify : publication authorized for current scope
final_verify -down-> gate : PASS
gate -[norank]-> implement : affected function needs repair\nthen new verifier
gate -down-> publish : PASS
publish --> [*] : commit-only / push-only / PR ready stop
publish -down-> merge : current PR ready + merge authorized
merge -down-> cleanup
cleanup -down-> done
done --> [*] : later functionality uses a new Plan

note right of expand
Same-requirement supplements update the original Ticket;
add a Ticket only for a distinct behavior boundary.
Independent requirements always start a new Plan,
even while another Plan is unmerged.
end note

note right of verify
The main agent directly dispatches fresh owners and verifiers.
Every worker is a leaf; no worker spawns another worker.
Codex uses fork_turns="none"; other hosts need equivalent fresh context.
All active roles count against actual host capacity; main + one worker needs two slots.
Dependent Tickets may prepare read-only; writes wait for prerequisite independent PASS.
Batch checkpoints preserve accepted state and all failure evidence.
end note

note right of final_verify
Normally a separate fresh verifier checks the entire current Plan scope.
One new Sol/high check may cover both gates only for one Ticket with identical
scope, artifact/version, configuration, and deployment surface.
Never reuse a verifier after scope or surface changes.
end note
@enduml
